From 57dfcfe03a348d08c7cea05d6eae7feb059abaa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:25:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: a drain of the FEL layer passes over an
 access unit whose base packet has not come

The video thread drains the decoders when the stream runs dry for ten frame
periods (a still frame, CVideoPlayerVideo::Process()), and the enhancement
layer is drained with the base layer. In a stream whose layers are coded in
different picture order, the access unit of the layer that a packet carries
can be the one of a base picture still to come. While the layer was drained,
such an access unit made it fail ("an enhancement picture has no base picture
at the end of the stream"), and the resynchronization that followed threw away
every enhancement picture already decoded for the base pictures still to come
out of their decoder: each of them went out without the FEL residual.

The access unit is now passed over: its base picture is not to come before the
end (a stream that goes on after a drain starts both decoders again,
CDrainRestart in DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg), and the drain goes on with the access
units after it. Those that refer to it are not given out by FFmpeg's HEVC
decoder, which makes no picture whose references are missing ("Error
constructing the frame RPS"), so their base pictures go out without the layer
and none is paired with a wrong picture; the others are paired. At the end of
a file every base packet has come, and nothing changes there.

Host test (fel_drain_test, BL_EL.mkv, a drain 20 packets after the start, the
layer paired): with the module before, a resynchronization and 2 pictures that
the drain gave out without the layer; with this one, no resynchronization and
1 (its enhancement access unit was in a packet that had not come).
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
index cf52e5e..a0a04c3 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
@@ -304,6 +304,8 @@ struct dvbridge_fel {
      * (dvbridge_fel_base_picture_rpu()) */
     unsigned layer_rpu_base, layer_rpu_none, layer_rpu_differ, rpu_lost;
     char reason_text[320]; /* a reason made for this failure (surface_reason()) */
+    /* Hades: access units of the layer that a drain passed over, their base packets not having come (pump()) */
+    unsigned drain_dropped;
 };
 
 /* Hades: whether two times are the same but for what a time may lose on its way here. */
@@ -1146,9 +1148,22 @@ static bool pump(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
         while (!timed && match < f->num_times && f->times[match].order != f->queue[0].order)
             ++match;
         if (!timed && match == f->num_times) {
+            /* Hades: while the layer is drained, the base packet of this access unit is not to come before the
+             * end (the video thread drains both decoders when the stream runs dry, and a stream that goes on
+             * after that starts both of them again: CDrainRestart). Its picture is not decoded, and the drain goes
+             * on with the access units after it, whose base pictures have come: those that refer to it do not
+             * come out of the decoder (FFmpeg's HEVC decoder makes no picture whose references are missing), and
+             * their base pictures go out without the layer; the others are paired. Before, the layer failed
+             * here, and the pictures it had decoded for the base pictures still to come out of their decoder were
+             * thrown away: every one of them went out without the layer. */
             if (f->draining) {
-                f->reason = "an enhancement picture has no base picture at the end of the stream";
-                goto fail;
+                ++f->drain_dropped;
+                f->packet_bytes -= packet->size;
+                av_packet_free(&f->queue[0].packet);
+                av_freep(&f->queue[0].rpu.data);
+                --f->num_packets;
+                memmove(f->queue, f->queue + 1, f->num_packets * sizeof(*f->queue));
+                continue;
             }
             break; /* A reference EL picture can precede its corresponding BL. */
         }
-- 
